From bec2e37ad98d256ab290cec962a6460f6b4af2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jelle Feringa <jelleferinga@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:47:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Define the bounds constructors of the joint velocity,
 acceleration and jerk constraints

The std::vector<Bounds> constructors were declared but never defined, so a
caller compiled and then failed to link. The bounds constructor now holds the
body and the targets constructor delegates to it with Bounds(t, t) per joint.
The jerk declaration takes std::string name like the other two.

The bounds are per step: the rows are finite differences of the positions,
not divided by a time step. A range bound stays a single row, which
TrajOptQPProblem does not accept; the doc says so.

Closes #606
